# {PROJECT_NAME}

A Glean agent built with the [Glean Agent Toolkit](https://github.com/gleanwork/glean-agent-toolkit).

## Setup

```bash
# Create a virtualenv
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate    # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate

# Install with your chosen framework's extras
pip install -e ".[{FRAMEWORK_EXTRA}]"

# Configure credentials
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env and fill in GLEAN_API_TOKEN and GLEAN_SERVER_URL
# (also fill in OPENAI_API_KEY / GOOGLE_API_KEY as appropriate for your framework)
set -a; source .env; set +a
```

## Run

```bash
python -m {PROJECT_MODULE}.agent_{FRAMEWORK_EXTRA}
```

Built-in tools enabled in this project: `{ENABLED_TOOLS_CSV}`

## Add a custom tool

```bash
/glean:add-tool my_tool --description "Does X" --params query:str
```

Custom tools live at `src/{PROJECT_MODULE}/tools/custom_tools.py`.

## Add another framework

```bash
/glean:add-adapter --framework langchain
```

This updates `pyproject.toml` and scaffolds `src/{PROJECT_MODULE}/agent_<framework>.py`.

## Diagnose

```bash
/glean:doctor              # check env, install, structure
/glean:doctor --probe      # also pings Glean (consumes API quota)
```

